---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import Navbar from "../../components/Navbar.astro";
import Footer from "../../components/Footer.astro";
import CtaBand from "../../components/CtaBand.astro";
import Comments from "../../components/Comments.astro";
import { whatsappLink } from "../../config";
---

<Layout
	title="How to Choose a Web Designer in Kenya: Scorecard (2026) | Orbit"
	description="Neutral scorecard to pick a web designer in Kenya: price, timeline, M-Pesa, speed, ownership, support — works on any quote."
>
	<Navbar />
	<main id="main">
		<section class="relative overflow-hidden border-b border-white/5">
			<div class="pointer-events-none absolute inset-0" aria-hidden="true">
				<div class="absolute -top-40 left-1/3 h-[400px] w-[600px] -translate-x-1/2 rounded-full bg-electric/15 blur-[80px] transform-gpu will-change-transform"></div>
			</div>
			<div class="relative mx-auto max-w-3xl px-5 pb-14 pt-20 md:pt-28">
				<p class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-electric">■ Guides · Choosing · 5 min</p>
				<h1 class="mt-4 text-4xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-white sm:text-5xl">
					Choosing a designer? <span class="text-gradient">Use this scorecard.</span>
				</h1>
				<p class="mt-5 text-lg text-slate-400">6 questions that work on any quote — including ours. Score 0–2 each.</p>
			</div>
		</section>

		<article class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-5 py-16">
			<p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-400">Choosing a web designer in Kenya is hard — everyone promises the same thing and prices range from KES 5k to 250k+. This scorecard gives you 6 objective questions to ask any designer (including us). Score each 0-2, then add up. Takes 5 minutes, saves you months of regret.</p>

			<div class="mt-8 grid gap-4">
				<div class="glow-border rounded-2xl p-6">
					<h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-white">1. Exact price in writing?</h2>
					<p class="mt-2 text-sm text-slate-400">0 = "it depends on your requirements", 1 = a range ("25k–50k"), 2 = fixed KES line-item with exactly what's included. A fixed price means they've done this before and know the work. A range means they'll surprise you later. Our prices: 35,999 / 47,999 / 59,999 — each with an exact deliverable list. Demand the same transparency from anyone.</p>
				</div>
				<div class="glow-border rounded-2xl p-6">
					<h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-white">2. Live date, not range?</h2>
					<p class="mt-2 text-sm text-slate-400">0 = "2–4 weeks", 1 = "about a week", 2 = "3–5 days Starter / 1 week Business / 2 weeks Master" with a written approval gate before launch. A date means they control their process. A range means they're guessing or juggling too many clients. Ask: "What specific date will my site go live, and what do I need to deliver by when?"</p>
				</div>
				<div class="glow-border rounded-2xl p-6">
					<h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-white">3. M-Pesa native or plugin?</h2>
					<p class="mt-2 text-sm text-slate-400">0 = "we'll add M-Pesa later" or "use Paystack", 1 = WooCommerce plugin, 2 = native Daraja API wiring (Till + Paybill) you can see in your own Safaricom portal. Plugin checkouts break on update, feel slow, and you don't own the flow. Ask to screen-share a test KES 10 payment — if they can't, they haven't built one.</p>
				</div>
				<div class="glow-border rounded-2xl p-6">
					<h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-white">4. Speed on cheap phone data?</h2>
					<p class="mt-2 text-sm text-slate-400">0 = "fast", no number, 1 = 70–89 PageSpeed, 2 = 90+ on <a href="https://pagespeed.web.dev" class="text-electric hover:underline">pagespeed.web.dev</a> mobile. Most Kenyans browse on 3G/4G, not fibre. A site that loads in 5 seconds loses 53% of mobile visitors. Ask for a live site URL to test yourself — never trust a screenshot.</p>
				</div>
				<div class="glow-border rounded-2xl p-6">
					<h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-white">5. Who owns what?</h2>
					<p class="mt-2 text-sm text-slate-400">0 = "we host it for you" (they own your site), 1 = "you own the domain", 2 = your domain + content + files + full license + M-Pesa credentials in your name. Read the terms before paying — some designers hold your site hostage when you leave. See our <a href="/terms-of-service" class="text-electric hover:underline">Terms</a> for an example of what fair looks like.</p>
				</div>
				<div class="glow-border rounded-2xl p-6">
					<h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-white">6. What happens after launch?</h2>
					<p class="mt-2 text-sm text-slate-400">0 = "good luck", 1 = "we're available if you need us", 2 = monthly care plan listed with hosting/security/backups/support and a reply-time SLA. A site without care rots — plugins go unpatched, SSL expires, speed decays. Ours: 7,499–13,999/mo, cancel anytime. Or DIY with the checklist in our <a href="/blog/website-care-kenya" class="text-electric hover:underline">Care guide</a>.</p>
				</div>
			</div>

			<div class="mt-8 rounded-xl border border-amber-500/20 bg-amber-500/5 p-5 text-sm text-slate-300">
				<p class="font-semibold text-white">Score: 10–12 = hire, 7–9 = ask more questions, &lt;7 = walk away.</p>
				<p class="mt-2 text-slate-400">Red flags: won't put price/date in writing, no PageSpeed number, "lifetime hosting free" (nobody gives free hosting forever), won't let you own domain/files, no post-launch support.</p>
			</div>

			<h2 class="mt-10 text-2xl font-bold text-white">Bonus: 3 questions to ask on the first call</h2>
			<ul class="mt-4 grid gap-3 text-sm text-slate-300">
				<li class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-electric">→</span> "Can you send me a live site you built so I can test it on my phone?" — Tests honesty and speed.</li>
				<li class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-electric">→</span> "What happens if I want to leave you after 6 months?" — Tests ownership and lock-in.</li>
				<li class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-electric">→</span> "Do you use native M-Pesa or a plugin?" — Tests technical depth.</li>
			</ul>

			<div class="mt-8 rounded-2xl border border-edge bg-panel p-6">
				<p class="text-sm font-semibold text-white">Challenge us</p>
				<p class="mt-1 text-sm text-slate-400">Send any competitor quote — we'll score both honestly, even if the answer is "they're fine, hire them." <a href={whatsappLink("Hi Orbit! I'm comparing designers — score my quote vs yours?")} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-electric hover:underline">WhatsApp the quote →</a></p>
			</div>
		</article>

		<Comments slug="best-web-designer-kenya" />
		<CtaBand title="Compare us live." text="No pitch — just numbers, side by side." />
	</main>
	<Footer />
</Layout>
